Z||000000||ChadMan||06-21-99||11:50 AM||||Just got back from a two-week vacation in which I delivered my father-in-law's 86 SE V6 automatic from Columbus, OH to Phoenix, AZ, stopping at historic Route 66 sites along the way.  We averaged 23 mpg and hit a top speed of 115 in the New Mexico desert (still accelerating when my wife made me slow down!).  Total repair bill for the trip:  8 bucks to plug a punctured tire.  What a great road car.<p>While in Phoenix we checked out PISA Corp.'s shop.  Items for sale included leather seat covers, digital dash kits, and a complete turn-key Artero conversion in pearlescent white with burgundy interior.  Fieralicious!
